  "body": "Was stacked on #798 (Tormach microARC 4, #785). #798 has merged, and upstream main (with the #844 build fix) is merged into this branch at `eb5bd15d`, so the diff is this PR's own 7 files.\r\n\r\nFork synced at v0.17.0 (process files PROCESS_VERSION 12).\r\n\r\n## What changed\r\n\r\nThe machine check judged a tilted move's canonical letters one by one. On the 770MX + microARC 4, whose only rotary is an A about X, it refused the face underneath (A0 B180) with \"states no B axis\". That table reaches the pose as A180, and the PathPilot post already posts it as `G0 A180`.\r\n\r\n- `crates/app/src/machine/judge.rs`: the pose gate moves here from `mod.rs` as `pose_problems`.\r\n  - On a machine with exactly one rotary, stated along X (the post's own test, x² ≥ 0.998·|d|²), the gate reads the tool angle about X from the letters. It uses the post's formula and tolerances (`tormach.cps` `toolAngle`), so the check and the post agree on every pose.\r\n  - The angle is signed by the stated direction (a `[-1,0,0]` table commands the negated angle, as the post writes the word) and judged against the rotary's travel.\r\n  - A pose with an X component, meaning any B or C a turn about X cannot make, is refused by name: `move i commands A .. B .. C .. deg; <model>'s only rotary, A about X, cannot reach that pose`.\r\n  - Every other machine keeps the letter law unchanged: none, two or more rotaries, or a single rotary that is unstated or not along X.\r\n- `crates/app/src/machine/mod.rs`: calls `pose_problems` instead of the inline letter loop. The file shrinks from 396 to 355 lines.\r\n- `assets/posts/fanuc.cps`: this post writes the stream's letters as they come (G43.4), so it now refuses a turning letter with no rotary of that name: `tilted move commands B - the machine states no B rotary`. Before this PR, the check stopped A0 B180 reaching that dialect on an A-only table. Now the post does, so the safety floor is unchanged.\r\n  - From the review: it also refuses a tilt on a lone rotary stated along -X (`tilted move on rotary A, stated along -X - ...`). The check judges that table by the negated angle; this dialect writes the letter unnegated, so A-45 on a `[-1,0,0]` 0..90 table would pass the check and post outside the travel. No shipped machine states a -X rotary, so no shipped output changes. Only a non-zero A is refused: A0 is the same word on either sign, so an upright section that states A0 still posts.\r\n- `assets/posts/doosan-dnm.cps` (delta review): the shipped DNM's A about X leans off Z, so the mirror sets `machine.rtcp` and Doosan's RTCP path writes the stream's letters raw. It now refuses, by name, the same two cases as Fanuc: a turning letter with no rotary of that name (so the A0 B180 the check now passes never posts a `B180` word to a machine with no B) and a non-zero A on a lone rotary stated along -X.\r\n- `judge.rs` doc: no longer claims every post agrees with the check. The PathPilot post does; the two G43.4 dialects (Fanuc, Doosan) write letters unnegated and refuse the B of A0 B180 and a turning A on the -X table by name.\r\n- `crates/app/tests/microarc_test_part.rs` (from #798): the wrap test now expects the post's refusal (`simultaneous 4-axis motion in operation WRAP`). It also asserts that the machine check no longer flags the wrap, whose every pose is reachable as an angle about X. The header comment is updated.\r\n- `docs/tester-kits/tormach-microarc-4th/README.md`: one sentence updated to match.\r\n- `docs/decisions/797-a-only-pose.md`: the decision record.\r\n\r\n## How tested\r\n\r\nThe new suite, `crates/app/tests/fourth_axis_pose.rs`, holds the pinning tests:\r\n\r\n- `an_a0_b180_slot_posts_as_a180_on_the_microarc4`: a real Slot with tilt A0 B180 on the bar job, built through the app's commands.\r\n  - The check is clean.\r\n  - `post_setup` writes exactly one index, `G0 A180`, and no B word.\r\n  - The cuts land on the skin (Z 0.375 → 0.36) inside the stick-out.\r\n- `the_face_underneath_is_judged_as_a180_against_the_travel`:\r\n  - With A travel -90..90, every move is refused as `commands A 180.000 deg (the pose A 0.000 B 180.000), the travel is -90.000..90.000`.\r\n  - A `[-1,0,0]` table commands -180: it passes on -180..0 and is refused on 0..180.\r\n- `a_pose_the_a_axis_cannot_reach_is_still_refused_by_name`: a B30 lean on the same machine is refused by name by the check, and `post_setup` refuses and writes no file.\r\n- `a_second_rotary_keeps_the_letter_law`: A about X plus C about Z still refuses B180 with `states no B axis`.\r\n- `the_fanuc_dialect_refuses_a_b_on_an_a_only_table`: fanuc.cps on the microARC mirror refuses A0 B180 by name and writes no `B180`. A90 posts.\r\n- `the_fanuc_dialect_refuses_a_lone_a_stated_along_minus_x`: on the microARC mirror stated `[-1,0,0]`, travel 0..90, fanuc.cps refuses A-45 by name and writes no `A-45`; stated `[1,0,0]` it posts A-45 as before.\r\n- `an_upright_a0_still_posts_on_a_minus_x_fanuc_table`: A0 on the -X table posts with no warning.\r\n- `the_doosan_dialect_refuses_a_b_on_its_a_only_table`: the shipped DNM passes the check on A0 B180; doosan-dnm.cps refuses the B by name and writes no `B180`. A90 posts.\r\n- `the_doosan_dialect_refuses_a_turning_a_stated_along_minus_x`: on the DNM stated `[-1,0,0]`, travel 0..90, A-45 is refused by name and no `A-45` is written; an upright A0 posts. Both Doosan tests fail against the previous `doosan-dnm.cps` (checked by running them on it). They live in `fourth_axis_pose.rs` beside the Fanuc ones, because `doosan_dnm_post.rs` would pass 400 lines.\r\n\r\nGate, on the merged tree `eb5bd15d` (main incl. #798 and the #844 fix):\r\n\r\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: app suites (the lib plus the gate-mapped `app::machine` suites, `fourth_axis_pose` among them) and ui suites, 477 passed, 0 failed.\r\n- Delta-review fix (693b2809), merged with upstream main at 7a7dba04 (only `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` conflicted; took main's 14): `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green, 482 passed, 0 failed. Run alone: `fourth_axis_pose` 9/9, `doosan_dnm_post` 7/7, `fanuc_post` 11/11, `machine` 33/33, `tormach_fourth_axis` 12/12, `microarc_test_part` 2/2, `conformance` 6/6, `index_swing` 9/9; `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\r\n- First review fix (d1c73221), run alone: `fourth_axis_pose` 6/6, `fanuc_post` 11/11, `machine` 33/33, `tormach_fourth_axis` 12/12, `microarc_test_part` 2/2, `conformance` 6/6, `index_swing` 9/9; clippy clean.\r\n- Before the review fix, run alone: `fourth_axis_pose` 5/5, `microarc_test_part` 2/2 (the kit golden now checks out LF, from #798's `.gitattributes` fix), `fanuc_post` 11/11, `tormach_fourth_axis` 12/12, `machine` 33/33.\r\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n\r\n- No real PathPilot or Fanuc control was run.\r\n- A refused tilt blocks the post in the app (`posting.rs`, `posting_per_op.rs`, `posting_mounts.rs` return \"post blocked\" on any counted warning), so no NC file is written. The dev CLI `crates/post/src/bin/post.rs` still writes the file and prints the warnings; left to the maintainer.\r\n- Doosan's indexing (non-RTCP) path was not changed: a -X rotary always leans off Z, so it always takes the RTCP path.\r\n- The release-lane `--ignored` heavy tests were not run.\r\n- The ui snapshot lane was not run.\r\n\r\nChangelog: The machine check reads a 4th-axis A-about-X table's pose through the tool axis, so the face underneath (A0 B180) posts as A180 on the 770MX + microARC 4; an unreachable pose is still refused by name, and the Fanuc post refuses a letter the machine has no rotary for.\r\n\r\nEffort: high\r\n\r\nFixes #797\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
